  "corpus": {
    "statement": "TEN DOCUMENTS IS THE CORPUS, and it stays ten until more notices are ingested. This is an enumeration, not an estimate. It was 8 until 2026-10-10: on 2026-09-30 all six sandbox MinIO buckets were listed in full (4061 objects), every PDF under every sustainment prefix was fetched and hashed, and the result was 8 distinct document contents with no unseen notice sitting in the bucket -- enumerated in docs/pcn-corpus-widening-2026-09-30.md. The corpus therefore does not widen by looking harder; it widens when new notices are ingested, which is exactly how it reached 10. TI PCN#20210316000.1 and IDT/Renesas PDN OV-19-05 were ingested into sustainment/inbound/ on 2026-10-10, the sustainment_sensor fired on both unaided, and both produced manifests under the versioned artifact layout.",
    "why_it_is_here": "This block exists so the denominator lives where the GATE READS IT rather than only in prose. pcn_corpus_run.check_ground_truth() asserts TARGETS against it at startup and aborts on a disagreement, and pcn_corpus_gate.py copies it into docs/corpus-gate/latest.json so a committed report states the corpus it was measured against. A denominator that only a human can check is a denominator that drifts.",
